Dear MSstats Developer<div><br><div>I am currently trying to reanalyze some data in preparation for a tutorial on msstatsTMT (Galaxy Tutorial with Melanie Föll).</div><div>I chose the small triple KO yeast experiment reanalyzed here:</div><div>&quot;

MSstatsTMT: Statistical detection of differentially abundant
proteins in experiments with isobaric labeling and multiple mixtures &quot;</div><div><br></div><div>I ran into 2 problems:<br></div><div>I think the Gigi lab annotation is incorrect, or my MaxQuant is counting the channels in a different way since the knockouts are clearly visible in different channels. To confirm this I wanted to have a look at your R scripts which should be available here:</div><div>  TKO-1mix data (MassIVE.quant reanalyses container identifier: RMSV000000267) </div><div>But the FTP does not seem to be public/available at least I cannot access it, although I can access other massive directories. Am I doing something wrong and other people can access it?</div><div><br></div><div>Could you please provide me with the complete data analysis of this part? The data is really nice and it would be awesome to have consistent data in these tutorials. </div><div><br></div><div>Best Klemens<br></div></div>
